---
import CaseStudyLayout from '../../components/CaseStudyLayout.astro';
import CaseStudyHero from '../../components/CaseStudyHero.astro';
import CaseStudySection from '../../components/case-study/CaseStudySection.astro';
import CaseStudySubsection from '../../components/case-study/CaseStudySubsection.astro';

const sections = [
	{ id: 'overview', label: 'Overview' },
	{ id: 'problem', label: 'Problem' },
	{ id: 'exploration', label: 'Exploration' },
	{ id: 'decision', label: 'Decision' },
	{ id: 'solution', label: 'Solution' },
	{ id: 'reflection', label: 'Reflection' },
];
---

<CaseStudyLayout title="Netflix — Julia Heo" sections={sections}>
	<CaseStudyHero
		logo="/images/netflix.png"
		logoAlt="Netflix"
		headline="Helping Netflix users spend less time choosing and more time watching"
		role="Personal Project"
		tags={['Product Design', 'Concept', 'Mobile']}
	/>

	<CaseStudySection id="overview" title="Overview">
		<CaseStudySubsection title="Netflix has thousands of options. Somehow, choosing one is still the hard part.">
			<p>Opening Netflix often starts the same way: scroll through a few rows, open a title, go back, and keep looking. When other people are involved, that indecision turns into a debate over everyone's moods, preferences, and time.</p>
			<p>I designed a lightweight recommendation flow that helps people narrow down what they want and arrive at one pick — whether they're watching alone or choosing with a group.</p>

			<div class="netflix-hero">
				<div class="netflix-hero__glow"></div>
				<div class="netflix-hero__stack">
					<div class="netflix-hero__side netflix-hero__side--left">
						<div class="netflix-hero__phone">
							<img src="/images/netflix/frame-112.png" alt="Netflix solo mood selection screen" loading="lazy" />
						</div>
                        <span> Solo </span>
					</div>
					<div class="netflix-hero__main">
						<div class="netflix-hero__screen">
							<img src="/images/netflix/frame-124.png" alt="Netflix recommendation for Minions based on solo viewing preferences" loading="lazy" />
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="netflix-hero__side netflix-hero__side--right">
						<div class="netflix-hero__phone">
							<img src="/images/netflix/frame-123.png" alt="Netflix group waiting screen showing submitted preferences" loading="lazy" />
						</div>
                        <span> Group </span>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</CaseStudySubsection>
	</CaseStudySection>

	<CaseStudySection id="problem" title="Problem">
		<CaseStudySubsection title="Netflix gives users plenty to watch, but not much help making the final decision.">
			<p>Existing recommendations still leave people comparing dozens of options. The interface is optimized for browsing, not for helping someone actually pick something to watch.</p>
			<p>The result is a familiar loop: open Netflix, scroll rows, open titles, back out, keep scrolling. Eventually, someone gives up and rewatches something they've already seen, or the group never actually starts the movie. </p>

			<div class="browse-loop">
				<div class="browse-loop__step">

                <div class="flow-step__screen">
						<img src="/images/netflix/Crop.png" alt="Choose viewing context" loading="lazy" />
					</div>
					<p class="flow-step__label"> Browse rows </p>

				</div>
				<span class="browse-loop__arrow">→</span>
				<div class="browse-loop__step">



                <div class="flow-step__screen">
						<img src="/images/netflix/open.png" alt="Choose viewing context" loading="lazy" />
					</div>
					<p class="flow-step__label"> Open title </p>


				
				</div>
				<span class="browse-loop__arrow">→</span>
				<div class="browse-loop__step">

                 <div class="flow-step__screen">
						<img src="/images/netflix/back.png" alt="Choose viewing context" loading="lazy" />
					</div>
					<p class="flow-step__label"> Go back </p>
					</div>


				<span class="browse-loop__arrow">↺</span>
				<div class="browse-loop__step">
                <div class="flow-step__screen">
						<img src="/images/netflix/scrolling.png" alt="Choose viewing context" loading="lazy" />
					</div>
					<p class="flow-step__label"> Keep scrolling </p>
					</div>
			</div>
			<p class="browse-loop__caption">More options → more comparison → more indecision → back to browsing.</p>
		</CaseStudySubsection>
	</CaseStudySection>

	<CaseStudySection id="exploration" title="Exploration">
		<CaseStudySubsection title="I started with a random movie generator.">
			<p>The first idea was simple: Netflix would choose something at random and remove the need to browse altogether.</p>
			<p>But pure randomness creates a different problem. It's fast, but it ignores why someone is watching, what they're in the mood for, and how much time they have. Users would probably keep regenerating results until something happened to feel right, which is basically browsing again! </p>

			

			<br> <blockquote class="pull-quote3">💡 So I shifted the concept from "pick something random" to "help me make a decision."</blockquote>
		</CaseStudySubsection>
	</CaseStudySection>

	<CaseStudySection id="decision" title="Decision">
		<CaseStudySubsection title="A few lightweight questions. One confident recommendation.">
			<p>The experience asks users a short sequence of questions, then recommends one title based on the answers.</p>

			<div class="flow-strip">
				<div class="flow-step">
					<div class="flow-step__screen">
						<img src="/images/netflix/frame-109.png" alt="Choose viewing context" loading="lazy" />
					</div>
					<p class="flow-step__label"> 01 Watching context</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flow-step">
					<div class="flow-step__screen">
						<img src="/images/netflix/frame-113.png" alt="Choose movie, series, or either" loading="lazy" />
					</div>
					<p class="flow-step__label"> 02 Content type</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flow-step">
					<div class="flow-step__screen">
						<img src="/images/netflix/frame-112.png" alt="Choose a viewing mood" loading="lazy" />
					</div>
					<p class="flow-step__label"> 03 Mood</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flow-step">
					<div class="flow-step__screen">
						<img src="/images/netflix/frame-114.png" alt="Choose a preferred watch length" loading="lazy" />
					</div>
					<p class="flow-step__label"> 04 Watch length</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flow-step">
					<div class="flow-step__screen">
						<img src="/images/netflix/frame-124.png" alt="Personalized recommendation result" loading="lazy" />
					</div>
					<p class="flow-step__label"> 05 Recommendation</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<p class="flow-strip__caption">Each question narrows the catalog without making the user build a detailed search.</p>
		</CaseStudySubsection>

		<CaseStudySubsection title="Key design decisions">
			<p>Six decisions shaped how the flow actually works, grouped by what they were trying to solve.</p>

			<h3 class="decision-row__heading">Row 1: Shaping the recommendation</h3>
			<div class="decision-grid">
				<div class="decision-card">
					<div class="decision-card__visual">
						<div class="mini-branch">
							<div class="mini-branch__box mini-branch__box--root">How are you watching?</div>
							<div class="mini-branch__connector"></div>
							<div class="mini-branch__lines">
								<div class="mini-branch__box mini-branch__box--leaf">Solo</div>
								<div class="mini-branch__box mini-branch__box--leaf">Group</div>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
					<p class="decision-card__title">Context first</p>
					<p class="decision-card__text">The first question ("How are you watching?") splits the flow immediately, so solo and group get different next steps.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="decision-card">
					<div class="decision-card__visual">
						<table class="decision-card__table">
							<thead>
								<tr><th>Genre</th><th>Mood</th></tr>
							</thead>
							<tbody>
								<tr><td>Comedy</td><td>Funny</td></tr>
								<tr><td>Animation</td><td>Comforting</td></tr>
								<tr><td>Thriller</td><td>Tense</td></tr>
							</tbody>
						</table>
					</div>
					<p class="decision-card__title">Mood over genre</p>
					<p class="decision-card__text">Different genres can satisfy the same mood. Framing the question around mood makes the interaction feel more natural and opens up cross-genre recommendations.</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<h3 class="decision-row__heading">Row 2: Reducing decision fatigue</h3>
			<div class="decision-grid">
				<div class="decision-card">
					<div class="decision-card__visual">
						<div class="mini-stack">
							<span class="mini-stack__chip">Mood</span>
							<span class="mini-stack__chip">Time</span>
							<span class="mini-stack__chip">Watching with</span>
						</div>
						<span class="decision-card__annotation">Only inputs that meaningfully change the result</span>
					</div>
					<p class="decision-card__title">Lightweight questions</p>
					<p class="decision-card__text">No actor filters, no release-year sliders — anything more turns a decision tool back into a search interface.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="decision-card">
					<div class="decision-card__visual">
						<div class="mini-fade">
							<div class="mini-fade__grid">
								<span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span>
								<span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span>
							</div>
							<span class="mini-fade__arrow">→</span>
							<div class="mini-fade__one"></div>
						</div>
						<span class="decision-card__annotation">Dozens of possibilities → one confident pick</span>
					</div>
					<p class="decision-card__title">One match</p>
					<p class="decision-card__text">A results list would return users to the same comparison loop the feature is meant to solve.</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<h3 class="decision-row__heading">Row 3: Making groups lightweight</h3>
			<div class="decision-grid">
				<div class="decision-card">
					<div class="decision-card__visual">
						<div class="mini-link">
							<span class="mini-link__chip">🔗 Invite link</span>
							<span class="mini-link__arrow">↓</span>
							<div class="mini-link__done">✓</div>
						</div>
						<span class="decision-card__annotation">Open link. Submit preferences. Done.</span>
					</div>
					<p class="decision-card__title">No profiles required</p>
					<p class="decision-card__text">Guests don't need Netflix accounts or manual setup from the host.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="decision-card">
					<div class="decision-card__visual">
						<div class="mini-waiting">
							<div class="mini-waiting__version mini-waiting__version--reject">
								<span class="mini-waiting__label">Rejected</span>
								<div class="mini-waiting__dots">
									<span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span>
								</div>
							</div>
							<span class="mini-waiting__arrow">→</span>
							<div class="mini-waiting__version mini-waiting__version--final">
								<span class="mini-waiting__label">Final</span>
								<span class="mini-waiting__count">3 submitted</span>
								<span class="mini-waiting__btn">Start</span>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
					<p class="decision-card__title">Host-controlled readiness</p>
					<p class="decision-card__text">Netflix can count submissions, but only the host knows when everyone is there.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</CaseStudySubsection>
	</CaseStudySection>

	<CaseStudySection id="solution" title="Solution">
		<CaseStudySubsection title="Five moments make up the full experience.">
			<p>Each step is deliberately short. The whole flow can happen in under a minute for solo viewers and a couple of minutes for groups.</p>

            <div class="split-flow">
				<div class="split-flow__top">
					<div class="split-flow__screen">
						<img src="/images/netflix/frame-109.png" alt="Choose solo or group viewing context" loading="lazy" />
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="split-flow__branches">
					<div class="split-flow__branch">
						<span class="split-flow__branch-label">Solo</span>
						<div class="split-flow__screen">
							<img src="/images/netflix/frame-112.png" alt="Select a mood for a solo recommendation" loading="lazy" />
						</div>
						<div class="split-flow__screen">
							<img src="/images/netflix/frame-124.png" alt="Solo recommendation result for Minions" loading="lazy" />
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="split-flow__branch">
						<span class="split-flow__branch-label">Group</span>
						<div class="split-flow__screen">
							<img src="/images/netflix/frame-117.png" alt="QR code and link for inviting a group" loading="lazy" />
						</div>
						<div class="split-flow__screen">
							<img src="/images/netflix/frame-122.png" alt="Group recommendation result for American Assassin" loading="lazy" />
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<h3 class="solution-block-heading">01 &nbsp; Choose the viewing context</h3>
			<div class="moment-layout moment-layout--split">
				<div class="moment-layout__primary">
					<div class="moment-layout__screen moment-layout__screen--large">
						<img src="/images/netflix/frame-109.png" alt="Initial solo or group selection" loading="lazy" />
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="moment-layout__secondary">
					<div class="moment-layout__screen">
						<img src="/images/netflix/frame-110.png" alt="Solo viewing path selected" loading="lazy" />
					</div>
					<div class="moment-layout__screen">
						<img src="/images/netflix/frame-116.png" alt="Group viewing path selected" loading="lazy" />
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
			<p class="moment-caption">One early choice keeps the solo experience fast while unlocking the extra steps groups need.</p>

			<h3 class="solution-block-heading">02 &nbsp; Set lightweight preferences</h3>
			<div class="moment-deck">
				<div class="moment-deck__card moment-deck__card--1">
					<img src="/images/netflix/frame-113.png" alt="Movie selected as the content type" loading="lazy" />
				</div>
				<div class="moment-deck__card moment-deck__card--2">
					<img src="/images/netflix/frame-112.png" alt="Comforting selected as the mood" loading="lazy" />
				</div>
				<div class="moment-deck__card moment-deck__card--3">
					<img src="/images/netflix/frame-114.png" alt="One to two hours selected as the watch length" loading="lazy" />
				</div>
			</div>
			<p class="moment-caption">Movie + comforting + 1–2 hours → Minions.</p>

			<h3 class="solution-block-heading">03 &nbsp; Bring the group together</h3>
			<div class="moment-sequence">
				<div class="moment-sequence__step">
					<div class="moment-sequence__screen"><img src="/images/netflix/frame-117.png" alt="Host invite QR code" loading="lazy" /></div>
				</div>
				<span class="moment-sequence__arrow">→</span>
				<div class="moment-sequence__step">
					<div class="moment-sequence__screen moment-sequence__screen--phone"><img src="/images/netflix/frame-118.png" alt="Guest mood preference screen" loading="lazy" /></div>
				</div>
				<span class="moment-sequence__arrow">→</span>
				<div class="moment-sequence__step">
					<div class="moment-sequence__screen"><img src="/images/netflix/frame-123.png" alt="Host sees how many guests submitted preferences" loading="lazy" /></div>
				</div>
			</div>
			<p class="moment-caption">The host shares a QR code or link. Everyone submits on their own device, and the host sees the count grow in real time.</p>

			<h3 class="solution-block-heading">04 &nbsp; One flow, two outcomes</h3>
			<div class="moment-final">
				<div class="moment-final__side">
					<span class="moment-final__label">Solo match</span>
					<div class="moment-final__screen"><img src="/images/netflix/frame-124.png" alt="Solo match for Minions" loading="lazy" /></div>
				</div>
				<div class="moment-final__side">
					<span class="moment-final__label">Group match</span>
					<div class="moment-final__screen"><img src="/images/netflix/frame-122.png" alt="Group match for American Assassin" loading="lazy" /></div>
				</div>
			</div>
			<p class="moment-caption">Same interface, same confidence — whether it's one person deciding or five.</p>
		</CaseStudySubsection>
	</CaseStudySection>

	<CaseStudySection id="reflection" title="Reflection">
		<CaseStudySubsection title="What I'd explore next">
			<p>This project stopped at a concept, but a few threads would be worth pulling on if it kept going.</p>

			<div class="reflection-grid">
				<div class="reflection-card">
					<span class="reflection-card__number">01</span>
					<p class="reflection-card__title">Test the question order</p>
					<p class="reflection-card__text">Does starting with mood feel faster than starting with content type?</p>
				</div>
				<div class="reflection-card">
					<span class="reflection-card__number">02</span>
					<p class="reflection-card__title">Explain the match</p>
					<p class="reflection-card__text">Show why Netflix selected the title without adding more decision-making.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="reflection-card">
					<span class="reflection-card__number">03</span>
					<p class="reflection-card__title">Handle disagreement</p>
					<p class="reflection-card__text">Explore one controlled alternative if the group rejects the first match.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</CaseStudySubsection>
	</CaseStudySection>
</CaseStudyLayout>

<style>
	/* Shared treatment for exported Netflix screens */
	.netflix-hero__screen,
	.netflix-hero__phone,
	.split-flow__screen,
	.flow-step__screen,
	.moment-layout__screen,
	.moment-deck__card,
	.moment-sequence__screen,
	.moment-final__screen {
		overflow: hidden;
	}
	.netflix-hero__screen img,
	.netflix-hero__phone img,
	.split-flow__screen img,
	.flow-step__screen img,
	.moment-layout__screen img,
	.moment-deck__card img,
	.moment-sequence__screen img,
	.moment-final__screen img {
		display: block;
		width: 100%;
		height: 100%;
		object-fit: cover;
	}

	/* Netflix hero composition */
	.netflix-hero {
		position: relative;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		padding: 40px 0;
		margin: 24px 0;
		overflow: hidden;
		border-radius: 16px;
		background: linear-gradient(180deg, #1a1a1a 0%, #0a0a0a 100%);
	}
	.netflix-hero__glow {
		position: absolute;
		top: 50%;
		left: 50%;
		transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
		width: 60%;
		height: 60%;
		background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(229, 9, 20, 0.35) 0%, rgba(229, 9, 20, 0) 70%);
		pointer-events: none;
	}
	.netflix-hero__stack {
		position: relative;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		gap: 24px;
		width: 100%;
		z-index: 1;
	}
	.netflix-hero__main {
		flex: 0 0 45%;
		z-index: 2;
	}
	.netflix-hero__screen {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		aspect-ratio: 16 / 10;
		background-color: #1f1f1f;
		border-radius: 12px;
		border: 0.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
		box-shadow: 0 24px 60px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
	}
	.netflix-hero__side {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 8px;
		flex: 0 0 20%;
		transform: translateY(20px);
	}
	.netflix-hero__phone {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		width: 100%;
		aspect-ratio: 9 / 19;
		background-color: #1f1f1f;
		border-radius: 14px;
		border: 0.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
	}
	.netflix-hero__label {
		font-family: 'Gabarito', sans-serif;
		font-size: 12px;
		font-weight: 500;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
	}
	.netflix-hero__placeholder {
		font-family: 'Gabarito', sans-serif;
		font-size: 12px;
		color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4);
		text-align: center;
		line-height: 1.4;
	}

	/* Split flow (Overview) */
	.split-flow {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 24px;
		margin: 32px 0 8px;
	}
	.split-flow__top { display: flex; justify-content: center; width: 100%; }
	.split-flow__branches {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
		gap: 32px;
		width: 100%;
		position: relative;
	}
	.split-flow__branches::before {
		content: '';
		position: absolute;
		top: -24px;
		left: 25%;
		right: 25%;
		height: 24px;
		border-top: 1.5px solid #E5E5E5;
		border-left: 1.5px solid #E5E5E5;
		border-right: 1.5px solid #E5E5E5;
		border-radius: 12px 12px 0 0;
	}
	.split-flow__branch {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 12px;
	}
	.split-flow__branch-label {
		font-family: 'Gabarito', sans-serif;
		font-size: 12px;
		font-weight: 500;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: #4483F0;
	}
	.split-flow__screen {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		width: 140px;
		aspect-ratio: 9 / 19;
		background-color: #f5f5f5;
		border-radius: 4px;
	}
	.split-flow__placeholder {
		font-family: 'Gabarito', sans-serif;
		font-size: 12px;
		color: #868686;
		text-align: center;
		line-height: 1.4;
	}
	.split-flow__caption {
		margin: 0 !important;
		font-family: 'Gabarito', sans-serif;
		font-size: 15px;
		color: #4a4a4a;
		text-align: center;
	}

	/* Browsing loop */
	.browse-loop {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 12px;
		margin: 32px 0 12px;
	}
	.browse-loop__step { flex: 1; }
	.browse-loop__screen {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		aspect-ratio: 16 / 10;
		background-color: #f5f5f5;
		border-radius: 12px;
	}
	.browse-loop__placeholder {
		font-family: 'Gabarito', sans-serif;
		font-size: 12px;
		color: #868686;
		text-align: center;
		line-height: 1.3;
	}
	.browse-loop__arrow {
		font-family: 'Gabarito', sans-serif;
		font-size: 20px;
		color: #4483F0;
		flex: 0 0 auto;
	}
	.browse-loop__caption {
		margin: 0 !important;
		font-family: 'Gabarito', sans-serif;
		font-size: 15px;
		color: #4a4a4a;
		text-align: center;
	}

	/* Before/after concept shift */
	.shift-compare {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 24px;
		margin: 32px 0;
	}
	.shift-compare__side {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 12px;
	}
	.shift-compare__label {
		font-family: 'Gabarito', sans-serif;
		font-size: 12px;
